## std.atomic — atomic types + memory ordering.
##
## Pass-through: real impl is zig's std.atomic. This file declares
## the zag-side type surface; the codegen router emits zig
## `std.atomic.*` calls for the actual load/store/cas operations,
## leaving the type names (`AtomicI32`, `Ordering.AcqRel`, …) as
## the user-facing API.
##
## AtomicPtr drops its type parameter for now — the parser doesn't
## yet support the `AtomicPtr<T>` declaration shape; the real
## codegen routes `std.atomic.AtomicPtr(*T)` via the concrete
## pointer type at the call site, which works without a generic
## declaration on the zag side.

pub struct AtomicI32  { _opaque: i32 }
pub struct AtomicI64  { _opaque: i64 }
pub struct AtomicUsize { _opaque: usize }
pub struct AtomicBool { _opaque: bool }
pub struct AtomicPtr  { _opaque: usize }

pub enum Ordering {
    Relaxed,
    Acquire,
    Release,
    AcqRel,
    SeqCst,
}
